                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "10f1bd46-268f-3eee-9706-3189dd594996",
                                        "entry_id": "e23ecf58-85d3-31f3-bc03-817af8aed721",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Resembling or characteristic of the Spanish chivalric hero Don Quixote; possessed with or resulting from the desire to do noble and romantic deeds, without thought of realism and practicality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6c2aac2-9eaf-4ce9-a825-a3783ebea4ca",
                                                "sense_id": "10f1bd46-268f-3eee-9706-3189dd594996",
                                                "text": "Olivier, as you know, was quixotic, and would not permit a secret service and spies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ca5e4fd-8225-4d0f-bc7c-8062a87ef0dc",
                                                "sense_id": "10f1bd46-268f-3eee-9706-3189dd594996",
                                                "text": "The message is not subliminal. […] Characters aren’t just quixotic, they cite Cervantes to one another."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23e55bc7-66e9-4f1d-b487-ab9001b31408",
                                                "sense_id": "10f1bd46-268f-3eee-9706-3189dd594996",
                                                "text": "The war triggered in [Miguel de] Unamuno the realization that, in hopeless times, quixotic lunacy could save people from the paralysis that often accompanies defeatism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8260578a-d4d2-4764-800c-3ccebf57ff61",
                                                "sense_id": "10f1bd46-268f-3eee-9706-3189dd594996",
                                                "text": "In the digital age, building a new library filled with old-fashioned printed books seems idealistic, almost quixotic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9902a7a4-86d7-33ab-89ae-1e61ff90fa80",
                                        "entry_id": "e23ecf58-85d3-31f3-bc03-817af8aed721",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Overly optimistic and moralistic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fce54a93-25d5-3b86-a98a-75f89c7449f9",
                                        "entry_id": "e23ecf58-85d3-31f3-bc03-817af8aed721",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Exceedingly idealistic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff63206b-67f1-41d9-8206-16acf14e5dd1",
                                                "sense_id": "fce54a93-25d5-3b86-a98a-75f89c7449f9",
                                                "text": "Call it a brain freeze, another 'Aleppo moment,' or a mere campaign stumble, but Gary Johnson has stumbled again in his quixotic presidential campaign."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
